id=a52sxq_storage
name=Galaxy A52s 5G StorageManagerService unblock
author=kusti420
description=StorageManagerService's handler thread hangs in H_SYSTEM_READY right after NandswapManager "Set daily quota" (in schedNextLimitReset/schedNextUpdateAverage -> JobScheduler.schedule), so it never processes user-unlock completion or H_BOOT_COMPLETED: "System unlocked users: []", emulated;0 never mounted (no /sdcard), setup wizard stuck. Make both NAND-swap job schedulers no-ops. The limit-reset job was the only thing that tops up the RAM Plus zram writeback quota (/sys/block/zram0/writeback_limit), so without it writeback would stop for good once the boot limit is used; schedNextLimitReset now starts K4NandswapQuota instead, which does the same top-up (NandswapManager.setDailyQuota(false)) once per 24 h of elapsed realtime from an hourly check on BackgroundThread, without JobScheduler. The bigdata average job stays off.
